as.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 48 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 8.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 5.7, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.7 to 8.9. December accounts for 6% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 3% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 6. Contract [1], for 14,970 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the limit threshold does not indicate improper conduct. It could reflect market pricing, budget constraints, or multiple separate needs. Statistical patterns alone do not prove wrongdoing in procurement processes.\nWhat can be checked: Check if multiple contracts under the limit cover the same service or supply. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same goods or services. Examine contract [1] to confirm if the amount was within budget and if the service was necessary.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["KAK92Ud1%2FKSzz8fXU2i3eQ%3D%3D","JHezLwv79YiAAM7L03kM8A%3D%3D","ZmV5LM76f2rua%2Fi14w%2FPLA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}